{"entryId":"1592","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:1592:1","sourceSha256":"64ba0f82a942cb2ed62e540da2468ecb634aafc5f9ae2e495820338e0289b56b","englishSha256":"0508c87640afdc5cb85271df4f7ebba054e8f5bc75b594ad3cc74c7714060f27","citations":[{"id":"1592:1:citation-01","he":[18,29],"en":[25,34],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Niddah_6b.7"},"reference":"Niddah 6b:7","assessment":"The Bavli gives Rav Tuvi bar Rav Katina and his four-loaf statement. Nedarim 12b:5 separately gives the same statement in the name of Rav Tuvi bar Kisna reporting Shmuel, which establishes a parallel, with the names and transmission chains left distinct.","evidence":[{"reference":"Niddah 6b:7","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Niddah_6b.7"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Nedarim 12b:5","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Nedarim_12b.5"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0],"holds":[],"notes":[{"text":"Niddah and Nedarim transmit parallel four-loaf reports with different names and chains. Preserve the exact Katina form here.","references":[],"urls":[]}],"comparisonEvidence":[{"reference":"Niddah 6b:7","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Niddah_6b.7"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Nedarim 12b:5","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Nedarim_12b.5"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"entryEvidence":[]}
